# Remote access

Remote access lets you monitor and control agent sessions on your device through the Pontia web dashboard. Agents, development tools, and project files continue to run and remain on that device.

## Enable remote access during setup

When `pontia init` prompts you to sign in and enable remote access, accept and complete the browser authorization. Continue through device registration to connect your device to Pontia Cloud. Pontia restarts the local service with the remote configuration and opens the Remote Dashboard for that device.

## Connect an existing installation

First, sign in:

```sh
pontia login
```

Pontia prints a verification address and a one-time code. Open the address in a browser, sign in with Google or GitHub, and approve the code. The CLI stores the resulting credential under your Pontia home directory.

Then register the current device:

```sh
pontia remote enable
```

Choose an available Edge and confirm the device name when prompted. Pontia generates the device identity used for end-to-end encrypted access and updates the running service when needed.

For registration without terminal prompts, use `pontia remote edges` to get an edge ID, then run `pontia remote enable --edge EDGE_ID --name "Device name"`. Both options are required. See [non-interactive initialization](/docs/initialization#non-interactive-initialization) for the full sequence and browser authorization requirements.

Open [app.pontia.dev](https://app.pontia.dev) to access your registered device.

## Check and manage the registration

Run this command on the device to compare its local identity with the Cloud registration:

```sh
pontia remote status
```

You can change the device's display name or Dashboard URL handle with `pontia remote edit`, and replace its encryption identity with `pontia remote rotate-key`. Cloud provides [Device settings](/settings/devices), [Session settings](/settings/sessions), and [Account settings](/settings/account). See [Device and account management](/docs/device-management) for the effect of each operation.

## Security model

The browser and your device establish an end-to-end encrypted session. The Edge carries the connection and relays ciphertext, while Pontia Cloud manages login, device registration, and access authorization.

Agent execution and project files remain on your device. See [Security](/docs/security) for protocol and credential details.

You may select an official Edge or [deploy a self-hosted Edge](/docs/self-hosted-edge). Both use Pontia Cloud for authorization; self-hosting lets you choose where ciphertext is relayed.

## Disable remote access

To unregister the current device and disable its remote access:

```sh
pontia remote disable
```

Local access remains available after remote access is disabled. For connection failures, see [Troubleshooting](/docs/troubleshooting).
